/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-138-  // covers cross-frame cell reads (a comprehension closure reading the
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-139-  // enclosing function's cellvar) without a narrowing-prone k-top redex
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-140-  // guarded on the FOUND frame's DECLARED cellvars (pnMember over the
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-141-  // cellsMark): decidable for every concrete frame pin — plain frames and
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-142-  // non-cell names prune outright, so an abstract looked-up value never
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-143-  // drags a narrowing cellV heap match along (probed on 5-intersperse and
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-144-  // Q4's abstract `numbers` in the annotated frame)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/core.k-145-  rule <k> #look(X:String, L:Int) => V ... </k>
